  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1149 AM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThe long term forecast will start off with warm and dry conditions \nWednesday and Thursday as the stubborn upper ridging will prevail. \nHeight and thickness increases will warm temperatures to the upper \n70s to lower 80s and precipitation chances near zero. At the same \ntime, the upper trough will finally push all the way onshore, \ndominating western CONUS. By the weekend, the upper ridging will \nfinally get with the program and shift east away from the forecast \narea. With the upper trough spanning across western to central \nCONUS, southwesterly flow will fill in aloft, ushering in \nsubtropical moisture to the mid to upper levels. Plenty of moisture \nand multiple passing shortwaves will bring potential for showers and \nthunderstorms everyday over the weekend and possibly early next \nweek. Daily precipitation chances and mostly cloudy skies will also \nslightly cool temperatures over the weekend.",
